From f1b0e8d0864de92bceeee470a9660905523c364e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dnz3d4c <dnz3d4c@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 21:59:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] Installer: install as a normal plugin, not a dev plugin

The plugin went into devPlugins and was enabled through DevPluginSettings.
That works, but Dalamud then reports it as a dev plugin, and the mod's own
plugin browser reads that state out loud - a released build should not
announce itself as somebody's work in progress.

It now goes where Dalamud puts a released plugin:

  installedPlugins\FF14Accessibility\<version>\FF14Accessibility.dll

Three details in that layout decide whether it loads at all, all verified
against Dalamud's own source rather than guessed:

- the version folder name must parse as a version. CleanupPlugins deletes
  every folder that does not, so an unreadable build manifest now stops the
  install instead of falling back to a placeholder name.
- the manifest needs InstalledFromUrl. LocalPlugin.IsOrphaned is true when
  no configured repository matches the manifest, and an orphaned plugin is
  skipped at boot - silently. "OFFICIAL" (SpecialPluginSource.MainRepo)
  makes the manifest non-third-party, so the main repository matches it.
- the profile entry has to carry the same WorkingPluginId as the manifest.
  Both sides are seeded here, and the id is carried across updates so
  repeated installs do not leave dead profile entries behind.

The dev-route leftovers are removed, not merely ignored: Dalamud loads dev
plugins and installed plugins in the same pass, so an old copy in devPlugins
would register the same command and the same hotkeys a second time.

vnavmesh keeps the dev route. Putting it in installedPlugins would mean
registering someone else's repository in the user's Dalamud settings, and
this project does not write into other people's configuration. DevMode is
therefore still switched on, but only when vnavmesh is actually there.

--install runs the whole thing without the window and sets an exit code, so
the install path can be checked automatically against a throwaway profile
root. The GUI is unchanged; it remains the path users take.
